<p>U.S. first lady Melania Trump will preside over a United Nations Security Council meeting in New York on Monday, the White House said—an unusual role for the spouse of a serving world leader. The White House said the session will focus on how education can promote tolerance and world peace, as the United States takes its turn holding the council’s rotating monthly presidency. The announcement also comes with extra attention because President Trump has long criticized the United Nations, including during his first term. For international observers, that makes a high-profile U.S. appearance at the council—led by the first lady—a notable diplomatic moment.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JjST5GCaH06jlAvbtLW2_jfBfSn2PFWNHJeQtLTt3TflOJxlF0Nytk-NhgxNZZbgHQvpARkwjE_lu9S7YdVTdjNO76VufP72eOBwjmNhoBjUoZ9xXNlLruJRbkC_Kifhu372u-2-SymW57urdskqzlPc-W02nYUvnNiFQb12kV1OCuXdigLTBmyriXqEB-kL-qBV4VkIOdZ9lWJhYdhkDPfvDANZTWSjk2cWE7cIBsgpGYFIztC5uhXCVAUFSkeVwWVV6RjIy3-coCgQ1Q' alt='FILE PHOTO: U.S. first lady Melania Trump attends a Governors Dinner hosted by U.S. President Donald Trump at the White House in Washington D.C., U.S., February 21, 2026. REUTERS/Aaron Schwartz/File Photo' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: The White House cast the meeting as a chance to highlight education’s role in building tolerance and world peace while the U.S. holds the Security Council presidency. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/politics/article/3344794/melania-trump-preside-over-un-security-council-meeting-white-house-says'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>The Globe and Mail: The outlet noted that President Trump has criticized the United Nations since his first term, giving the announcement additional context. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-melania-trump-un-security-council/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/politics/article/3344794/melania-trump-preside-over-un-security-counci